Unlike the native `keyof` keyword, which returns keys present in **all** union members, this type returns keys from **any** member.

@link https://stackoverflow.com/a/49402091

@example
```

import type {KeysOfUnion} from 'type-fest';

type A = {
common: string;
a: number;
};

type B = {
common: string;
b: string;
};

